165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (This project presents a complete predictive analytics study for forecasting monthly electricity demand of a utility / power distribution company for the upcoming year. Using a sample historical dataset covering January 2021 to December 2025, the study applies multiple data mining techniques available in IBM SPSS Modeler. The work follows the CRISP-DM methodology and demonstrates an end-to-end workflow from data understanding to deployment-ready forecasts.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Four modeling approaches were implemented and compared: \(1\) Multiple Linear Regression, \(2\) CHAID Decision Tree, \(3\) Multilayer Perceptron Neural Network, and \(4\) Time Series Expert Modeler. Key predictors include average temperature, industrial and residential usage, holiday indicators, economic conditions, seasonality, and lagged demand values.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
